#N canvas 20 20 2300 2500 12;
#X text 20 20 c_devid -- ONE DEVICE'S ANSWER TO A UNIVERSAL DEVICE INQUIRY \, and nothing else. It watches the SysEx stream for a reply whose manufacturer byte matches its creation argument and bangs once per matching frame. Instantiated once inside each m_ layer that polls \, which is why it is a c_ rather than a u_: there is more than one., f 84;
#X text 20 170 creation arg 1: the MANUFACTURER BYTE to match -- byte 5 of the reply \, counting the leading F0 as byte 0. REQUIRED. inlets: none -- it owns its own [sysexin]. outlet 1: a bang per matching reply., f 84;
#X text 20 290 ⛔ IT EXISTS BECAUSE ONE [sysexin] HEARS EVERY DEVICE. Until the nano and the 404 were polled \, only the Launchpad ever sent SysEx in this rig -- measured -- so m_launchpad could treat ANY SysEx as proof of its own presence \, and its comment said exactly that. The moment all three are polled all three reply \, and that shortcut would report the Launchpad present whenever the NANO answered: item 235 silently un-fixed \, in the worst direction \, because the watchdog would believe a device that is gone., f 84;
#X text 20 470 THE BYTE THAT TELLS THEM APART \, all three measured -- item 249 \, and the Launchpad's is item 98:, f 84;
#X text 20 530 Launchpad Pro MK3 -- F0 7E 00 06 02 [00] 20 29 23 01 00 00 00 04 06 05 F7 -- arg 0 \, Novation., f 84;
#X text 20 580 nanoKONTROL ------- F0 7E 00 06 02 [42] 04 01 00 00 23 00 00 00 F7 -------- arg 66 \, KORG., f 84;
#X text 20 630 SP-404MKII -------- F0 7E 10 06 02 [41] 08 04 00 00 00 03 00 00 F7 -------- arg 65 \, Roland., f 84;
#X text 20 700 ⚠️ ARG 0 IS THE WEAKEST OF THE THREE \, and it is worth knowing why rather than discovering it. A manufacturer byte of 00 means A THREE-BYTE ID FOLLOWS \, so 0 does not identify Novation -- it identifies the whole class of manufacturers who ran out of one-byte ids. It is unambiguous HERE because the Launchpad is the only such device in the rig. A second one would need bytes 6 and 7 matched as well \, which is two more boxes and no new idea., f 84;
#X text 20 880 ⚠️ [sysexin] HAS A PORT OUTLET \, AND IT IS DELIBERATELY NOT USED YET. Pd 0.49's [sysexin] is byte then PORT -- measured by connecting each outlet in turn \, with outlet 5 tried first to prove the probe could fail at all. A port gate would be exact where a manufacturer byte is merely sufficient. ⬜ What is NOT measured is whether that outlet counts from 0 or from 1 \, which cannot be established on a Mac with no MIDI input open. See ref/module/presence.md., f 84;
#X text 20 1060 ⚠️ REALTIME BYTES ARE FILTERED \, and this is not theoretical: u_tempo puts 96 clock bytes a second on the wire and anything >= 248 is legal in the middle of a SysEx stream. Counting them as frame bytes would put the manufacturer byte at the wrong index and the match would fail intermittently \, at a rate that depends on the tempo. lib_grid.py skips them for the same reason on the way out., f 84;
#X text 20 1230 THE MODEL IS THREE RULES AND NO collecting FLAG. On F0 the index and the match both clear \; on byte 5 the match is set if it equals the argument \; on F7 a set match bangs and then clears. A stray F7 with no F0 in front of it cannot bang \, because nothing set the match -- which is what the flag would have been for., f 84;
#X text 20 1400 THE TRIGGER IS t f b f f AND THE ORDER IS THE DESIGN. Rightmost first: the F0 reset \, then the byte into a cold store \, then the bang that advances the index -- so the compare at index 5 reads a byte that is already parked -- and the F7 test last of all., f 84;
